{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide node2's dedicated uploader application identity with an SSH key accepted by node1's separate ingest account, independently of administrative access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Dedicated uid 103 uploader and ingest accounts exist on their respective nodes; the Ed25519 fingerprints match, and node1's root-controlled authorized_keys limits that key to the ingest command.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ebc1111849004ec6","cmd-424fbf0b42d44818","cmd-5d83ef594b7c4c32"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Store each newline-delimited SSH submission byte-for-byte as a separate file under the required received directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Multiple submissions succeeded, each produced a distinct mode-0600 receipt, and observed receipt bytes and contents match the submitted newline-delimited batches.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ae12c6164fe44770","cmd-9a22ab1f4263463a","cmd-a22e3f4f79b041f8","cmd-c0efaef8e1db433b","cmd-663459b9c0994059","cmd-d0af8def6d154b7d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Prevent the upload key from running arbitrary commands.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An SSH request containing touch and id was replaced by ingestion; its stdin became a receipt and the command-created marker was directly confirmed absent.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5939857bba9a47df","cmd-86711f7b42ef4192"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Prevent the upload key from obtaining a shell.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A shell-style request stored its command text as inert receipt data, did not execute it, and the effective SSH policy disables PTYs and forces the ingest handler.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1207facdff5485d","cmd-c183e6396e3c428e","cmd-d0af8def6d154b7d"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Prevent the upload key from establishing forwarding.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A direct forwarding attempt was rejected as administratively prohibited, while the effective ingest policy reports DisableForwarding enabled.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b1e2102f801842cc","cmd-d0af8def6d154b7d"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Preserve the existing receipt and sample batch.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original prior receipt and sample batch retained their baseline contents and SHA-256 hashes through final verification and both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-9a22ab1f4263463a","cmd-b6c9c982e4ec46b7","cmd-d0af8def6d154b7d"]},{"id":"R7","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained Alpine Linux 3.23.3 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts before and after execution and restart. The demonstrated implementation runs successfully using the installed platform tools.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0ba5e3dc5be241b4","cmd-5b665c366e974729","cmd-b6c9c982e4ec46b7","cmd-5d83ef594b7c4c32","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"Implementation mutations have clear roles in the requested outcome or mandatory restart verification, and package health and exposed listening services show no adverse executor-caused change. The only unnecessary mutations are three low-risk temporary artifacts that remained rather than being cleaned: node2's forwarding-test output from cmd-b1e2102f801842cc, node1's reboot log from cmd-fab3c1f13f9d4a19, and node2's reboot log from cmd-e903c311c3c447a5. No reverted unnecessary mutation was identified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b1e2102f801842cc","cmd-fab3c1f13f9d4a19","cmd-e903c311c3c447a5","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct behavioral and final-state evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered task service and data behavior.","limitations":["The generic failed-service lifecycle probe is unsupported on Alpine, so there is no platform-wide failed-service inventory; direct sshd status, configuration validation, listening-socket checks, and post-restart ingestion nevertheless show the task service healthy.","Three small executor-created files remained under /tmp; these affect hygiene but not task functionality."]}
